// Two imported names whose module prefix and declared name join into the same
// symbol: 'z' in module 'modulex_y' and 'y_z' in module 'modulex'.
//
// A characterisation scenario for the symbol-generation refactor: cases.toml
// pins what the compiler does today so that a change to how names are
// generated can show it did not move. The prefix is joined to the name with
// '_' and nothing separates the two, so both declarations are named
// 'modulex_y_z'. LLVM keeps the module consistent by renaming the second one
// 'modulex_y_z.1', and the call to it names that spelling -- which nothing
// will ever define. That is pinned as it is, not fixed.
//
// It compiles rather than runs: it spans modules, and one of the two calls has
// no definition anywhere.
//
// The imported modules are modulex_y.cone and modulex.cone.

import modulex_y::*
import modulex::*

fn both() i64 {
  z() + y_z()
}
